1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,637
This is the submission for challenge
three: a GLP-1 receptor agonist.

2
00:00:05,637 --> 00:00:13,938
Twenty de-novo designs, seven method families, one ranked file
— and one method that ranks them: an activation-geometry gate.

3
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,175
The brief asks for an agonist, not a binder.

4
00:00:18,175 --> 00:00:24,262
Confirmed binders go into a receptor-activation
assay, and only a confirmed agonist counts.

5
00:00:24,262 --> 00:00:32,338
GLP-1 itself runs from the peptide groove of the extracellular
domain, along the junction toward the transmembrane bundle.

6
00:00:32,338 --> 00:00:38,450
A design that only caps the groove is the classic
antagonist — so the designs must span the path.

7
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:49,600
The target: human GLP-1R, the challenge segment 24 to 432,
scored against the active-state reference structure 6X18.

8
00:00:49,600 --> 00:01:06,775
The amber residues are the message region of GLP-1 — arginine 190, tyrosine 148,
tryptophan 306, glutamine 234, and glutamate 387, plus the third extracellular loop.

9
00:01:06,775 --> 00:01:11,588
A design has to engage them, at
the depth GLP-1 itself reaches.

10
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,625
We score activation geometry explicitly.

11
00:01:15,625 --> 00:01:34,288
Six contacts — an anion to R190, an aromatic at Y148, a small group at W306, a hydrogen bond to
Q234, a hydrophobe at E387, and ECL3 — plus how deep the ligand inserts below the vestibule rim.

12
00:01:34,288 --> 00:01:41,975
The cutoffs are fixed in the published tool, so before trusting
it we reproduced its calibration on four experimental structures.

13
00:01:41,975 --> 00:01:45,887
GLP-1 scores six of six
at twenty-one ångströms.

14
00:01:45,887 --> 00:01:48,887
Exendin-P5, four of six.

15
00:01:48,887 --> 00:01:51,188
Exendin-4, four of six.

16
00:01:51,188 --> 00:01:54,062
And the weak partial agonist, one of six.

17
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:58,862
The designs come from seven
independent method families.

18
00:01:58,862 --> 00:02:03,438
RFdiffusion3 mini-proteins targeted
at the groove and the junction.

19
00:02:03,438 --> 00:02:07,700
BoltzGen cyclic peptides at the
junction, and two shorter peptides.

20
00:02:07,700 --> 00:02:10,075
EvoBind, from sequence alone.

21
00:02:10,075 --> 00:02:12,000
One BindCraft2 peptide.

22
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:18,312
And two SolubleMPNN families that re-sequenced
the strongest backbones with the interface pinned.

23
00:02:18,312 --> 00:02:25,000
Every backbone was re-folded against the full receptor
— five samples each — and every sample was scored.

24
00:02:26,467 --> 00:02:30,617
Here they are, one by one: the
whole submission in ranked order.

25
00:02:30,617 --> 00:02:37,792
Each design  is shown in its predicted pose on the receptor
— the binder in pink, the  interface residues in amber.

26
00:02:37,792 --> 00:02:42,242
Watch the groove and the junction:
the strongest  designs reach both.

27
00:02:42,242 --> 00:02:48,804
The first rows carry the full six-of-six pharmacophore
at  depth; then the strongest five-of-six binders.

28
00:02:48,804 --> 00:02:54,767
Twenty designs, seven method  families,
all sequences unique, no near-duplicates.

29
00:03:06,467 --> 00:03:08,904
The first three rows carry the rubric.

30
00:03:08,904 --> 00:03:16,292
The EvoBind peptide c2-run1-b206 hits
all six contacts at GLP-1's own depth.

31
00:03:16,292 --> 00:03:23,854
The RFdiffusion3 mini-protein e1-r0025
has the strongest interface in the set.

32
00:03:23,854 --> 00:03:29,717
And the BoltzGen peptide c8-run13 combines
six of six with a two-domain hit.

33
00:03:29,717 --> 00:03:40,254
Every design carries three recorded screens — fold confidence, interface score, and
hydropathy — and the organisers' own prescreen found no known binder among them.

34
00:03:41,567 --> 00:03:42,754
One honest limit.

35
00:03:42,754 --> 00:03:49,992
Activation cannot be predicted from a co-fold: the gate scores
the pose it is given, not whether the design adopts it.

36
00:03:49,992 --> 00:03:54,417
Pose agreement across the five samples
is the mitigation — not a proof.

37
00:03:54,417 --> 00:03:57,579
And the binding affinities
are for the assay to decide.

38
00:03:58,867 --> 00:04:08,879
That is the submission: twenty designs, seven method families, ranked by activation
evidence first, prescreen clean, with the full method in the methodology text.

39
00:04:08,879 --> 00:04:10,279
The assay decides.
